# Local overrides for working inside example/ (Beacon). Copy to .env (gitignored)
# and uncomment what you want. Command-line args still win, e.g. make serve PORT=9001.
# Plain KEY=value (read by `make`); no quotes, no `export`. This is the example's
# OWN .env, separate from ../.env, so its PORT stays clear of the root site's.

# Container engine — auto-detected (podman, else docker). Force one:
# ENGINE=docker

# Preview server (make serve): host interface + port (8001 keeps it clear of root's).
# BIND=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8001

# Branch that `make publish-to-branch` commits the built site to (push separately).
# BRANCH=gh-pages
